# Supabase RLS — required on every new table

Every `CREATE TABLE` in `public` that lives in a Supabase migration MUST also:

1. `ALTER TABLE <table> ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;`
2. Include AT LEAST one `CREATE POLICY ... ON <table>` covering `SELECT`. Add separate policies for `INSERT` / `UPDATE` / `DELETE` (or one combined `FOR ALL`) as needed.

This is non-negotiable. The product_effect_sequences table shipped with RLS enabled but no policies, which silently returned zero rows to the SSR client and caused multi-shot fireworks to fire only one shot in the preview. We do not want that class of bug again.

## Standard patterns in this codebase

- **Catalogue / shared reference data** (e.g. `effect_specs`, `catalogue_products`, `product_effect_sequences`): authenticated users can read; only the `admin.manage_catalogue` permission can write.

  ```sql
  ALTER TABLE public.<table> ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

  CREATE POLICY <table>_select_authenticated
    ON public.<table>
    FOR SELECT
    USING (auth.uid() IS NOT NULL);

  CREATE POLICY <table>_admin_write
    ON public.<table>
    FOR ALL
    USING (public.has_permission(auth.uid(), 'admin.manage_catalogue'))
    WITH CHECK (public.has_permission(auth.uid(), 'admin.manage_catalogue'));
  ```

- **Per-user data** (e.g. `shows`, `show_cues`, `shopping_list_items`): scope by `auth.uid()` against the owning user/show.

  ```sql
  CREATE POLICY <table>_owner_all
    ON public.<table>
    FOR ALL
    USING (user_id = auth.uid())
    WITH CHECK (user_id = auth.uid());
  ```

## Review checklist

When reviewing a migration PR, confirm:

- [ ] Every new table has `ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`.
- [ ] Every new table has at least one `CREATE POLICY ... FOR SELECT` (or a `FOR ALL` policy that covers it).
- [ ] Write paths are gated by an explicit permission check or ownership check.
- [ ] The migration filename version (the prefix before the first `_`) is unique across the `platform/supabase/migrations/` directory.

If a table is intentionally meant to be queryable by anonymous users, document why in a SQL comment immediately above the policy.
